the dup is certainly a party in disarray  deeply divided by the brutal manner by  which arlene foster was  deposed as party leader at the end of  april they say be careful what you wish  for  edwin putz had aspirations of leadership  for many years  he co-led the coup against her but he  discovered when he got the new job that  it came with all the same old  challenges a party boxed in with no room  for compromise  because of the existing unionist anger  over the brexit border in the irish  sea so just 21 days into the job he's  been overtaken by events and forced to  resign  and that could have very serious  implications for the power sharing  government here  at stormont i've just heard in the last  few minutes that tomorrow's  north south ministerial council meeting  is unlikely to take place and that is  not a good sign  the dup were not happy that the british  government had  granted sinn fein's request to legislate  for irish language  rights at westminster if it didn't  happen here they told edwin putz not to  nominate paul given his first minister  but he went ahead and did that anyway so  you've now got to wonder how  tenable the new first minister's  position is if he resigns to  power sharing goes with him just one  other thing to wonder about tonight and  that is  who might become the new leader remember  edwin puts one by 19 votes  to 17 it was very close the other  contender  sir jeffrey donaldson the man who leads  the party at westminster  he was giving nothing away when he left  party headquarters this evening  but he's got to be the front runner to  be the third dup leader  in the space of two months
 

